<p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary/80 font-medium italic mb-8 border-l-4 border-secondary pl-6">Recovery after jaw surgery is not random. It follows a predictable arc, and the small choices you make each day have an outsized effect on the final result.</p>
<p><strong>Recovery time after jaw surgery is typically 6 to 12 weeks for the visible healing phase, with the final bite and facial result settling over 6 to 12 months.</strong> Most patients return to desk work in 1 to 2 weeks, resume a soft-chew diet by week 3, and chew normally by week 6. The first week is the most demanding, the second to sixth weeks bring steady improvement, and the months that follow are about fine-tuning the bite and waiting for sensation to normalise.</p>
