<h2 id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 font-headline-md text-primary mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="not-prose space-y-4 mb-12">
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">When can I return to work after jaw surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Desk work: 1 to 2 weeks. Light physical work: 3 to 4 weeks. Heavy physical work: 6 weeks. Plan to work from home for the first week if possible — fatigue is significant in the first 7 to 10 days and remote work lets you rest between focused blocks.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">When can I return to college or school after jaw surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Most students return to college or school by week 2, once swelling and energy levels allow. Avoid heavy backpacks, contact sport, and noisy canteens with hard-to-chew food for the first 3 weeks. Talk to your surgeon about an extended leave or hybrid attendance if exams fall in the first 4 weeks.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">When can I eat normal food after jaw surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Liquids (weeks 0 to 2), soft-chew (weeks 3 to 6), normal chewing (week 6 onward). Hard, crunchy, or sticky foods should wait until week 10. Most patients eat a normal home-cooked Indian meal — rice, dal, sabzi, soft roti — by week 8.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">When can I brush my teeth normally after jaw surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">From week 2, brush inner and biting surfaces gently with a soft brush. Normal brushing of all surfaces resumes from week 3 to 4, after the suture review. Avoid electric toothbrushes on the incision lines for the first 3 weeks, and continue chlorhexidine rinses twice a day until week 4.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">When can I exercise or play sports after jaw surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Walking from day 0. Light cardio from week 2 to 3. Running, swimming, and yoga from week 4 to 6. Heavy lifting and contact sports from week 10 to 12. Always wear a custom mouth-guard for any contact sport after surgery — the plates and screws inside the jaw are strong, but a direct blow still risks damage to the healing bone.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">When can I drive after jaw surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Once you are off opioid painkillers and can turn your head, check mirrors, and react quickly — usually around week 1 to 2 for most patients. Start with short, familiar routes and avoid peak-hour traffic for the first week of driving.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Will I have visible scars after jaw surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">In most modern jaw surgery, all cuts are made inside the mouth — there are no visible scars on the face. A small subset of cases (some lower-jaw advancements, some chin procedures, some trauma repairs) need a small external incision under the jaw or in a natural skin crease. These incisions are typically 2 to 4 cm long and fade to a near-invisible line over 6 to 12 months with proper scar care.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">When can I exercise after jaw surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Walking immediately. Light cardio at 2 to 3 weeks. Heavy lifting and contact sport at 6 weeks minimum, ideally 10 to 12 weeks.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">When does the swelling fully resolve?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Most swelling is gone in 4 to 6 weeks. Subtle residual swelling can last 3 to 6 months.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">How long does numbness last after jaw surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Most numbness improves over 3 to 6 months. Small areas of altered sensation can last up to a year. Permanent complete numbness is rare.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Will I be on a liquid diet the whole time?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">No — liquids transition to soft foods by week 3, and a near-normal diet by week 6.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">Will I need to have elastics between my jaws?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Usually yes, for the first 1 to 2 weeks. They guide the bite and are removed gradually.</p></details>
<details class="group border border-surface-container-high rounded-xl bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 cursor-pointer open:bg-surface-container-low transition-colors shadow-sm"><summary class="font-headline-sm text-primary text-[18px] flex justify-between items-center list-none font-semibold">How do I open my mouth after surgery?<span class="material-symbols-outlined group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform text-secondary">expand_more</span></summary><p class="mt-4 font-body-md text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">Begin gentle jaw-opening exercises from week 2. Your surgeon and physiotherapist will guide you.</p></details>
